{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said, etc., at the border of the land of Edom, etc.</b> The reason it was necessary to say <b>at the border</b>, etc.: it means, on account of their reaching the border of wickedness, Aharon was taken. Furthermore, a midrash came to my hand (Yalkut Shimoni Numbers §764) and this is its language: ״בְּהִתְחַבֶּרְךָ לָרָשָׁע״ (when you join the wicked), etc. — because they joined with Edom they lost one righteous person, end quote. And these are the very same things we hinted at in the phrase <b>at the border</b>, etc. And according to this approach, the saying of <b>לֵאמֹר</b> (to say) is explained: that HaShem commanded Moses to say to Israel this specific point hinted at in the phrase ״at the border״ — that their joining with the wicked caused the passing of the righteous one. And even though this decree had already been decreed upon him, it is possible that he would have lived yet more days. Further, they say: ״they roll the liability through the hand of the guilty.״" "And by way of allusion (remez): since Aharon stands with Moses for the future redemption, as they of blessed memory said (Shabbat 10a) concerning the verse ״וְעָנְתָה שָּׁמָּה כִּימֵי נְעוּרֶיהָ״, as I have written above, and the future redemption is immediately from Edom, which is the kingdom of Samael, therefore it says <b>at the border of the land of Edom</b> — meaning, on account of the border that HaShem set as the end for Edom, to deliver it into Israel's hand; therefore there Aharon would be gathered. And the verse concludes <b>to his people</b>, to allude to his people who are destined to inherit the land of Edom."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:11:28.952922542Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}